# Lessons Learned

This machine was an excellent introduction to chaining multiple vulnerabilities together.

Key takeaways:

* Always investigate anonymous FTP access.
* Backup files often contain sensitive information.
* Source code review can reveal credentials and authentication logic.
* MD5 hashes are weak and commonly crackable.
* SQL Injection is often only the beginning of an attack path.
* Application source code frequently contains reusable credentials.
* Stable access is often more valuable than a temporary shell.
* Always run `sudo -l`.
* Misconfigured sudo permissions are one of the most common privilege escalation vectors.

