# Final Thoughts

Vaccine is one of my favorite Starting Point machines because it demonstrates how seemingly small findings can be chained together into full system compromise.

A simple anonymous FTP login led to source code disclosure, which led to credential recovery, SQL Injection, command execution, credential reuse, SSH access, and finally privilege escalation to root.

This machine reinforces an important lesson:

> Enumeration wins boxes.

